{"resourceIdentifier":"3627","resourceName":"Eastern Cape Restoration Project, South Africa - Makhanda","description":"The Eastern Cape Restoration Project is a revegetation project, aimed at the landscape restoration of the native Albany thicket, within a biodiversity hotspot that has undergone extreme degradation and ecosystem loss. A multi-year drought, combined with a multiple decades of over grazing have led to a scenario whereby vast areas of land can no longer support either economic or ecological functions. The project restores ex-grazing lands with a native species, Portulacaria afra, which shows unique ecological features adapted to the semi-arid project area. Planted at high density and subsequently protected from grazing, the restoration activity facilitates a microclimate and dense canopy cover that subsequently allows for the return of the high floral biodiversity endemic to the project area. The project is a grouped project covering the sub-municipality of Makana and is implemented hand in hand with the Eastern Cape Restoration Project, South Africa - Somerset East, and the Eastern Cape Bamboo Forestry Project, for the creation of a holistic restoration strategy.","location":{"latitude":33.239615,"longitude":26.335131},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2022-08-19","endExclusive":"2022-09-19","endInclusive":"2022-09-18"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"3627"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Eastern Cape"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"EcoPlanet Bamboo Group, LLC"},{"type":"string","value":"DE, United States"},{"type":"string","value":"+254-721-999-604"},{"type":"string","value":"crebelo@ecoplanetbamboo.com"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","va